From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:15:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: starfive: visionfive2: SPL hints for the mmc pins

U-Boot v2025.10 dropped the bootph-pre-ram hints for the mmc0/mmc1 pin
groups together with the support for the deprecated SD card and eMMC boot
modes. In SD card boot mode the boot ROM still starts the SPL from the
card, but the SPL then fails with "spl: partition error" because it cannot
read the card. Add the hints back for the VisionFive 2 boards.
---
 .../dts/starfive-visionfive2-u-boot.dtsi      | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/dts/starfive-visionfive2-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/riscv/dts/starfive-visionfive2-u-boot.dtsi
index 4c86d28..f3d7272 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/dts/starfive-visionfive2-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/dts/starfive-visionfive2-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -15,4 +15,29 @@
 	assigned-clock-rates = <0>; /* FIXME: delete property and implement cpufreq */
 };
 
+/*
+ * SD card and eMMC boot modes (RGPIO1:0 = 0:1 / 1:0): the boot ROM loads the
+ * SPL from the card, and the SPL needs the mmc pins to load u-boot.itb from
+ * it. Upstream dropped these hints when it deprecated those boot modes.
+ */
+&mmc0_pins {
+	bootph-pre-ram;
+
+	mmc-pins {
+		bootph-pre-ram;
+	};
+};
+
+&mmc1_pins {
+	bootph-pre-ram;
+
+	clk-pins {
+		bootph-pre-ram;
+	};
+
+	mmc-pins {
+		bootph-pre-ram;
+	};
+};
+
 #include "starfive-visionfive2-binman.dtsi"
-- 
